---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SystemDiagram from '../components/diagrams/SystemDiagram.astro';
import ModelShowcase from '../components/home/ModelShowcase.astro';
import {MODEL_SPECS} from '../data/model-specs';
import {SITE_URL} from '../config/site';
const steps=[
['01','Understand your outage needs','Decide what must stay powered and how long your typical outage lasts.','/guides/first-time-buyer-guide/'],
['02','Build your load profile','Record real nameplate loads and motor-starting requirements before choosing a kW number.','/planning/sizing/'],
['03','Plan generator capacity','Compare essential-load, unmanaged and load-managed scenarios without hiding unknowns.','/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/'],
['04','Compare brands','Narrow the field by documented product families, warranty terms and local service questions.','/brands/'],
['05','Compare exact models','Check fuel-specific output, transfer equipment, documentation and evidence gaps.','/models/'],
['06','Understand installed cost','Separate the generator from site work, fuel, electrical, permits and commissioning.','/cost/standby-generator-cost/'],
['07','Choose a fuel path','Compare natural gas and propane around availability, storage, consumption and outage resilience.','/guides/natural-gas-vs-propane/'],
['08','Plan the installation','Check placement, transfer equipment, local approvals and qualified-trade responsibilities.','/installation/'],
['09','Normalize installer quotes','Make missing scope, exclusions and apples-to-oranges differences visible before comparing totals.','/planning/quotes/'],
['10','Verify serviceability','Confirm who commissions, maintains and supports the exact system before you sign.','/research/local-service/']
];
const trust=[
['Exact-model research','Fuel-specific ratings and package variants stay attached to exact configurations.'],
['Primary-source evidence','Manufacturer manuals and official sources are identified where available.'],
['Unknowns stay unknown','Conflicts and missing evidence are shown instead of silently filled in.'],
['No invented testing','Desk research is never presented as hands-on testing or licensed trade review.']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Whole House Generator Buying Guide" description="Research home standby generators with clear comparisons, installation cost guidance, sizing information, and practical advice before speaking with an installer." schema={{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebSite',name:'Standby Generator Guide',url:SITE_URL+'/'}}>
<section class="cinematic-home-hero" aria-labelledby="home-hero-title">
  <div class="cinematic-hero-image">
    <img
      src="/images/user-editorial/premium-home-at-dusk.webp"
      width="1536"
      height="1037"
      alt="Warmly lit American home at dusk with a residential standby generator beside the house"
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>
  <div class="cinematic-hero-shade" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cinematic-hero-layout editorial-container">
    <div class="cinematic-hero-copy">
      <p class="cinematic-hero-eyebrow">INDEPENDENT RESEARCH <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> FOR U.S. HOMEOWNERS</p>
      <h1 id="home-hero-title">Independent Home Standby Generator Buying Guide for Whole House Generators</h1>
      <p class="cinematic-hero-lede">Research home standby generators with clear comparisons, installation cost guidance, sizing information, and practical advice before speaking with an installer.</p>
      <nav class="cinematic-hero-actions" aria-label="Start your generator research">
        <a class="cinematic-hero-button cinematic-hero-button-primary" href="/guides/">Explore Generator Guides <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="cinematic-hero-button cinematic-hero-button-outline" href="/brands/">Compare Generator Brands <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="cinematic-hero-button cinematic-hero-button-outline" href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">Understand Installation Costs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
      <p class="cinematic-hero-editorial">Source-linked desk research · No sponsored rankings · No claims of hands-on testing</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cinematic-hero-bottom">
      <p><span>THE HOMEOWNER FIELD GUIDE</span> Research the whole system, not just the generator.</p>
      <a href="#quick-start-heading">Start with the essentials <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="editorial-container py-9 sm:py-14" aria-labelledby="quick-start-heading">
  <div class="mb-6">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE 60-SECOND START</p>
    <h2 id="quick-start-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary sm:text-3xl">Three questions before you choose a generator</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-gray-700">You do not need to understand every generator specification today. Start with the answer you need; move into exact-model evidence only when you are ready.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">01 · SIZE</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">What size do I need?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Plan the circuits that matter and record real equipment loads. Square footage alone is not a sizing method.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/">Start with sizing →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">02 · COST</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">How much will it cost?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Understand equipment versus installed price, site work, gas and electrical scope before comparing bids.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">See installed cost factors →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-[#cbd5cf] bg-[#f4f8f5] p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#315647]">03 · CHOOSE</p>
      <h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold leading-snug text-primary">Which model fits my home?</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Compare exact fuel ratings, switch packages, warranty documents and who will service it locally.</p>
      <a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-[44px] items-center font-bold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/comparisons/five-brand-standby-generator-comparison/">Compare five brands →</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-600">Already have competing bids? <a class="font-semibold text-primary underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4" href="/planning/quotes/">Compare three installer quotes side by side →</a></p>
</section>


<ModelShowcase />

<section class="showcase-editorials" aria-label="Homeowner research highlights">
  <div class="editorial-container">
    <div class="showcase-section-heading showcase-editorials-intro">
      <div><p class="showcase-eyebrow">02 / Understand the project</p><h2>Beautiful equipment.<br /><em>Thoughtful planning.</em></h2></div>
      <p>A generator is only one part of backup power. Learn the home-specific decisions that matter before comparing installation proposals.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="showcase-editorial-grid">
      <article class="showcase-story showcase-story-primary">
        <a href="/installation/generator-pad-and-placement/" class="showcase-story-image" aria-label="Read the generator placement and pad guide">
          <img src="/images/user-editorial/landscaped-generator-placement.webp" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Landscaped area beside a house showing the setting for a residential standby generator" />
          <span class="showcase-story-image-label">THE INSTALLATION / 01 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
        </a>
        <div class="showcase-story-copy">
          <p class="showcase-eyebrow">Site, placement &amp; safety</p>
          <h3>Where it goes matters as much as what it does.</h3>
          <p>Explore clearances, site preparation, drainage, exhaust direction and the questions a qualified installer must answer.</p>
          <a href="/installation/generator-pad-and-placement/" class="showcase-text-link">Explore placement research <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="showcase-story">
        <a href="/cost/standby-generator-quote-checklist/" class="showcase-story-image" aria-label="Read the installation quote checklist">
          <img src="/images/user-editorial/generator-quote-review-at-home.webp" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Homeowner at a table reviewing a written standby-generator quote and project notes" />
          <span class="showcase-story-image-label">THE INVESTMENT / 02 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
        </a>
        <div class="showcase-story-copy">
          <p class="showcase-eyebrow">Cost, scope &amp; ownership</p>
          <h3>Know what you're buying before you sign.</h3>
          <p>Check equipment, transfer switches, fuel work, permits and commissioning against the same line-item scope.</p>
          <a href="/cost/standby-generator-quote-checklist/" class="showcase-text-link">Open the quote checklist <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="showcase-disclosure">Photographs are illustrative editorial visuals, not verified photographs of the model configurations shown above or evidence of field testing.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="editorial-container py-10 sm:py-14" aria-labelledby="research-topics-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">START WITH YOUR QUESTION</p>
  <h2 id="research-topics-heading" class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary sm:text-3xl">Whole house generator research, in decision order</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-gray-600">Find the cost of a whole house generator, compare generator brands and sizing options, or understand what installation involves. These are educational guides—not installer listings or claims of hands-on testing.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator cost →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Equipment prices, installed-price ranges and what changes a quote.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator sizing →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Running loads, motor starts, fuel ratings and load-management choices.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/installation/what-to-expect/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Whole house generator installation →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Assessment, transfer equipment, permits, fuel work and commissioning.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/comparisons/five-brand-standby-generator-comparison/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Best whole house generator? →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Compare five brands by exact-model evidence, local service and system fit.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/comparisons/generac-vs-kohler/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Generac vs. Kohler →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Two 26 kW-class configurations, fuel-specific output and ATS scope.</span></a>
    <a class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 hover:border-accent" href="/brands/kohler/"><span class="block text-lg font-semibold text-primary">Kohler whole house generators →</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-gray-600">Compare documented 26RCA/26RCAL packages, ratings and warranty terms.</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="premium-trust-strip" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
  <div class="editorial-container">
    <div class="premium-trust-layout">
      <figure class="premium-trust-visual">
        <img src="/images/user-editorial/generator-pad-site-assessment.webp" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Illustrative generator-site assessment beside an American house with plans and prepared pad" />
        <figcaption class="premium-trust-photo-credit">A SYSTEM-WIDE VIEW <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> INSTALLATION CONTEXT</figcaption>
        <div class="premium-trust-visual-caption">
          <span>01 / RESEARCH PRINCIPLES</span>
          <strong>Look beyond the brochure.</strong>
          <small>Real decisions require traceable information and clear limits.</small>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <div class="premium-trust-content">
        <div class="premium-section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">WHY TRUST THE RESEARCH</p>
          <h2 id="trust-title">Evidence first.<br /><em>Confidence second.</em></h2>
          <p>We separate manufacturer facts, homeowner planning assumptions, editorial interpretation and evidence we still need to verify.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="premium-trust-grid">
          {trust.map(([title,body], index) => (
            <article class="premium-trust-card">
              <span class="premium-trust-index" aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <h3>{title}</h3>
              <p>{body}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="premium-method-note">
      <div class="premium-method-stat"><span>{MODEL_SPECS.length}</span><div><strong>Tracked configurations</strong><small>Including documented package variants</small></div></div>
      <p>Research-based guidance only. No hands-on generator testing claimed; technical professional review remains pending.</p>
      <a href="/review-process/">How we verify information <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="editorial-container premium-journey" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
  <div class="premium-journey-intro">
    <div class="premium-journey-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">THE HOMEOWNER DECISION PATH</p>
      <h2 id="journey-title">Ten clear steps.<br /><em>One confident decision.</em></h2>
      <p>A premium standby-power system starts with the right questions, not a brand logo or headline kW number. Follow the whole project, from your home's loads to the installer who will support it.</p>
      <a class="premium-journey-start" href="#journey-steps">Explore the 10-step plan <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="premium-journey-visual">
      <img src="/images/user-editorial/selective-power-during-outage.webp" alt="Illustrative home with essential circuits illuminated during an outage" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      <figcaption>ILLUSTRATIVE BACKUP SCENARIO <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <div id="journey-steps" class="premium-journey-board">
    <div class="premium-journey-board-heading">
      <span>THE FIELD GUIDE <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> ALL TEN DECISIONS</span>
      <span>05 PHASES · 10 STEPS</span>
    </div>
    <ol class="premium-journey-list">
      {steps.map(([n,title,description,href], index) => (
        <li class="premium-journey-item">
          <a href={href}>
            <span class="premium-step-number" aria-hidden="true">{n}</span>
            <span class="premium-step-main">
              <span class="premium-step-phase">{['DEFINE YOUR NEEDS','DEFINE YOUR NEEDS','PLAN THE SYSTEM','PLAN THE SYSTEM','COMPARE THE OPTIONS','COMPARE THE OPTIONS','PREPARE THE PROJECT','PREPARE THE PROJECT','VERIFY THE PROPOSAL','VERIFY THE PROPOSAL'][index]}</span>
              <strong>{title}</strong>
              <small>{description}</small>
            </span>
            <span class="premium-step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="premium-journey-footnote">A planning sequence, not a substitute for a qualified site assessment, electrical design or permit review.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="premium-system-band" aria-labelledby="power-architecture-title"><div class="editorial-container premium-system-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE POWER ARCHITECTURE / EXPLAINED</p><h2 id="power-architecture-title">Not just a generator. <em>An entire home power system.</em></h2><p>Two power sources, one transfer decision, and carefully planned circuits. Explore how the equipment works together—and why a successful backup-power project starts with the whole system.</p><ul class="premium-link-list"><li><a href="/installation/automatic-transfer-switch-guide/">How the automatic transfer switch works →</a></li><li><a href="/sizing/generator-load-management/">How load management changes sizing →</a></li><li><a href="/sizing/whole-home-vs-essential-loads/">Whole-home vs essential-load backup →</a></li></ul></div><div class="premium-diagram-shell"><SystemDiagram/></div></div></section>

<section class="editorial-container premium-feature-grid" aria-label="Research tools">
  <article class="premium-feature premium-feature-image"><img src="/images/sizing-electrician-panel.webp" width="720" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Electrician evaluating a residential electrical panel for generator planning" /><div><p class="eyebrow">SIZE WITH CONTEXT</p><h2>Build the load plan before choosing capacity.</h2><p>Work through heating, cooling, pumps, kitchen, laundry and special loads. Unknown inputs remain explicit so a planning estimate does not masquerade as a measured home load.</p><a class="button" href="/planning/sizing/">Start guided sizing →</a></div></article>
  <article class="premium-feature premium-feature-image"><img src="/images/cost-install-quote.webp" width="720" height="480" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Homeowner reviewing an itemized standby generator installation proposal" /><div><p class="eyebrow">THE QUOTE DESK</p><h2>Compare scope, not just totals.</h2><p>Normalize generator, ATS, fuel, electrical, site work, permits, commissioning, warranty, maintenance, taxes and exclusions across three proposals.</p><a class="button" href="/planning/quotes/">Compare installer quotes →</a></div></article>
</section>

<section class="premium-final-cta"><div class="editorial-container"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU SIGN</p><h2>Turn research into questions your installer must answer.</h2><p>Bring the same load assumptions, exact equipment identifiers and scope checklist to every proposal. That is how a homeowner gets a cleaner comparison.</p></div><div class="premium-final-actions"><a class="button" href="/cost/standby-generator-quote-checklist/">Open the quote checklist →</a><a href="/models/">Browse exact model research</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>